# The M6 composed die: the pipped cube (21 balls, one group cut)
# filleted IN PLACE — twelve box-edge blends with every pip rim
# carried through as a ring, then all 21 rims replaced by slit-seamed
# torus bands. Four elementary surface kinds in one solid (plane,
# cylinder, sphere, torus), every carrier a line or a circle, meeting
# along TANGENT trimlines; the bands' slit meridians are Seam edges.
#
# Kernel counts are 89 faces / 195 edges / 129 vertices. OCC keeps
# the faces and vertices and splits periodic carriers at their seams
# (the filleted_die/ball/donut accounting), so its edge count exceeds
# the kernel's. The volume is the Pappus closed form
# (Steiner blank − 21·(cap + rim-torus term)) — FreeCAD's own measure
# reproduces it to sub-mm³ on a ~0.95 m³ body.
#
# KERNEL_* pin the NATIVE body's census and certified volume, full
# precision (the literal is the export writer's round-tripping float
# printer's output; crates/step-export/tests/kernel_sidecars.rs asserts
# these lines against the live kernel). scripts/check_step.sh consumes
# EXPECT_* (what FreeCAD/OCC reports after import) and ignores KERNEL_*.
KERNEL_SOLIDS=1
KERNEL_SHELLS=1
KERNEL_FACES=89
KERNEL_EDGES=195
KERNEL_VERTICES=129
KERNEL_VOLUME_MM3=952914984.0146472
EXPECT_SOLIDS=1
EXPECT_SHELLS=1
EXPECT_FACES=89
EXPECT_EDGES=245
EXPECT_VERTICES=129
EXPECT_VOLUME_MM3=952914984
